[
    {
        "content": "<p>Do we have graded posets? I'm in particular interested in the theorem that any finite bounded distributive lattice can be uniquely graded such that the grade of bot is 0 and the grade of top is <code>Set.ncard {x | SupIrred x}</code>.</p>",
        "id": 616367194,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1786641605
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>wdyt about</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- A `β`-rank function on an order `α` is a function `α → β` respecting the less-than relation and</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">the covering relation. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrderRank</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">RelHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CovBy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CovBy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">protected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">strictMono'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">StrictMono</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsGradableOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nonempty_orderRank</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">OrderRank</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 616402690,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786653077
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This looks sufficient for my use case, in which <code>α</code> is a finite partial order and <code>β</code> is <code>Nat</code>. I've never actually encountered gradings before I found out I wanted this theorem so I can't comment on anything else.</p>",
        "id": 616403585,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1786653459
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Order.krullDim#doc\">docs#Order.krullDim</a> not suffice for your theorem?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DistribLattice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BoundedOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">krullDim</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SupIrred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ncard</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Also I'm not sure but <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=OrderEmbedding.supIrredLowerSet#doc\">docs#OrderEmbedding.supIrredLowerSet</a> might be related<br>\n(see point 2 in the module docstring: \"Any nonempty finite distributive lattice is isomorphic to the lattice of lower sets of its partial order of sup-irreducible elements.\")</p>",
        "id": 616408414,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786655340
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This guarantees that <em>some</em> chain has length <code>{a : α | SupIrred a}.ncard</code>, but not that <em>every</em> maximal chain does so. Also, this doesn't give me the rank function, and it also doesn't tell me that if <code>x</code> covers <code>y</code> then the rank of <code>x</code> is one more than the rank of <code>y</code>.</p>",
        "id": 616409179,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1786655668
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In algebra there is the concept of a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catenary_ring\">catenary ring</a> and it feels like you're trying to write down what the prime ideals of this ring look like. As far as I know we didn't get this far in algebra, but historically it seems that when we run into concepts like this in commutative algebra the first thing to do is to develop the abstract order theory preliminaries.</p>",
        "id": 616409859,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1786655967
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/graded.20poset/near/616409179\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>but not that <em>every</em> maximal chain does so.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><code>DistribLattice</code> implies <code>IsWeakUpperModularLattice</code>, which implies all maximal chains have the same cardinality.</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/graded.20poset/near/616409179\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Also, this doesn't give me the rank function,</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Order.height#doc\">docs#Order.height</a></p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/graded.20poset/near/616409179\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>and it also doesn't tell me that if <code>x</code> covers <code>y</code> then the rank of <code>x</code> is one more than the rank of <code>y</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Sure but that could be a theorem</p>",
        "id": 616409875,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786655973
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yes, this sounds like it could be a better idea then, for my use case</p>",
        "id": 616410685,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1786656292
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110038\">Kevin Buzzard</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/graded.20poset/near/616409859\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In algebra there is the concept of a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catenary_ring\">catenary ring</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Cool! I believe this should be <code>IsJordanDedekindOrder (HeightOneSpectrum R)</code> once we have <code>IsJordanDedekindOrder</code> (or maybe using <code>Set.ofPred Ideal.IsPrime</code> instead of <code>HeightOneSpectrum</code>?), although I'm still confused about Jordan-Dedekind <a href=\"https://math.stackexchange.com/questions/890247/definition-of-jordan-dedekind-chain-condition\">vs</a> Jordan-Hölder</p>",
        "id": 616410820,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786656342
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=GradeOrder#doc\">docs#GradeOrder</a> what you want?</p>",
        "id": 616444640,
        "sender_full_name": "Noah Walker",
        "timestamp": 1786673853
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>oh yeah that does look like what I want</p>",
        "id": 616444717,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1786673907
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>oh wow</p>",
        "id": 616444728,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786673912
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I wonder do they have the theorems</p>",
        "id": 616444762,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1786673929
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>They don't seem to have many theorems, though the original <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib3/pull/11308\">PR</a> mentions cool applications</p>\n<p>We could show these as a start:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">GradeMinOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grade</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">height</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">GradeMinOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grade</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">height</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">GradeMinOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">grade</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Order</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">height</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 616446746,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1786675270
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is pretty new to me, so I am learning by trying examples... now I wonder why I don't see many instance in mathlib like this</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DivisionRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GradeMinOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Submodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"